        "description": "reported C observation; not an independent validation"
      },
      "text": "The sale list: `borg_think_shop_sell()` sets `sold_item_num` to the\n  index just written (not a count), and every reader (here and in\n  borg-store-buy.c) scans `p < sold_item_num`, so the most recent sale is\n  never seen. `sold_item_nxt` wraps at 9, so slot 9 is never used.\n  borg-store-buy.c does the same with its `bought_item_*` list."
    },
    {
      "group": 34,
      "reference": {
        "role": "borg_rs",
        "repository": "diegoami/borg-rs",
        "commit": "c375a82456741f7e4d4d410b27390ba68077ba9c",
        "path": "docs/c-bugs.md",
        "start": 639,
        "end": 643,
        "description": "reported C observation; not an independent validation"
      },
      "text": "`bought_item_num` is the index of the last entry written, but the\n  readers (`borg_store_sell`) loop `p < bought_item_num`, so the latest\n  purchase is never checked; `bought_item_nxt` wraps at 9, so entry 9 is\n  never used. (`sold_item_*` in borg-store-sell.c work the same way and are\n  read the same way here.)"
    }
  ],
